  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Shu'ayb: no motif. No earthquake, bodies or destruction drawn; wind only for «كأن لم يغنوا فيها». Their claim (90:7-12) is framed «هذا ما سولت لهم أنفسهم». STAGING v4: Shu'ayb is named but not drawn (not placed in the scene). 90: the chiefs who disbelieved (three faceless men in dark robes) speak (90:1) to the people of the town (three faceless men, left), the camera on the chiefs (90:3); both groups turn (90:5-6) and leave the stage on 90:7, before the chiefs' conditional saying (90:7-12) is recited, so no gesture is acted inside it and the street is empty long before 91:1. 91: the quake shakes the empty town (91:2 to 92:1): no body, no ruin, day (not dawn). 92 (as though they had never lived there): the wind blows through the empty street with a wind plate (92:4-7, after Shu'ayb's name and ending before it again) and a few leaves."
